{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review","id":1536743,"title":"W5 Scent Of Decay - Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-03T08:02:57-07:00","id":1536743,"title":"W5 Scent Of Decay - Review","content":"I had some time yesterday, so I bought the Scent of Decay book and dug into it.<br /> <br /> Scent of Decay presents itself as a chronicle book that takes starting-characters and introduces new STs and players to various elements of W5 through three adventures. And then there\u2019s an appendix at the end with some smaller scenes that you supposedly can use to create moments that explain raises in Renown.<br /> <br /> But first, you have\u2026<br /> <br /> (Also, <b>spoiler-warning</b> for the events in the particular adventures)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter One: Assembling The Pack</span><br /> <br /> This chapter tries to act like it will help with introducing the framework of the campaign and offers some tips and guidelines for a Session Zero. You get a section on Session Zero, Conflict In The Pack and Building Up Your Packmates.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem here is that it\u2019s all very surface-level. And this wouldn\u2019t be that big of a deal. After all, this is supposed to be a starter-chronicle. Since it could not just be an introduction for the players but a person\u2019s first attempt at being the ST as well. But the problem is that the advice is so surface-level that there\u2019s a lot of overlap with the W5 corebook. Even if we talk about an ST who\u2019s just a beginner. The least you can expect is that this person has also read the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that due to the rather surface-level approach, it misses a lot of the intricacies of the WtA-setting. For example, in the secton on \u201cConflict In The Pack\u201d it offers this: \u201cThe ahroun is just about to rip apart the employee of an oil company when the philodox intervenes, arguing that killing defenseless people is not what the Garou are supposed to do.\u201d And that\u2019s it. It doesn\u2019t really get into the roles the Auspices have and how that figures into the group-dynamic of the PC-Pack. The closest it comes when it later talks about Galliards: \u201cOne auspice excels above all others when it comes to building up their packmates. That one is obviously galliard. When your job is to tell the stories of your pack at the moot, you have a wonderful opportunity to build up your friends in ways that support their character concepts. It doesn\u2019t have to be all that complicated: Simply make their successes sound as grand as possible, ideally in line with their character concepts.\u201d But it just isn\u2019t enough to offer anything of much use (especially in light of what you already get from the W5 corebook). And how Tribes play into these group-dynamics doesn\u2019t get discussed, at all, for example. Like how does it figure into a group\u2019s dynamic to have a Glass Walker and a Red Talon in one group? It would have been more worthwhile to delve into that instead of the very surface-level discussion of Session Zero and group dynamics that happens here.<br /> <br /> Then it has a list of \u201cUnusual Packs\u201d and with that it presents the idea of Packs where all the PCs have the same Auspice. So, you get five Pack-types here for each Auspice. The most interesting one, I think, is the All-Philodox-one which is called \u201cRebuilding the Nation\u201d and it\u2019s described like this: \u201cThe Garou Nation is in tatters, destroyed by the internal divisions among werewolves. Yet the dream of being united against the Wyrm still lives and is the purpose of this traveling pack consisting of a few philodoxes and their packmates. They move from sept to sept, trying to heal old wounds and get intransigent elder werewolves to talk to each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> Visually this is presented as if it\u2019s on a page. Even though it\u2019s more of a sidebar. You\u2019d think it would reserve these kinds of backgrounds for in-character text that you could use as a handout during the game\u2026 but no. Instead, sometimes you have sidebars that just get these fancier backgrounds for really no reason. It\u2019s on odd choice.<br /> <br /> Next it presents the setting for the chronicle: Milton. It\u2019s supposed to be a midwestern small town in the US. And the assumed standard for the PCs is \u201chuman-born and working class\u201d. There\u2019s a few example origin-stories listed \u201cYou tried to get a job but didn\u2019t.\u201d, \u201cYou got a job as security guard but then got fired.\u201d, \u201cYou try to get by stealing stuff from big corporations and supermarkets.\u201d. Somehow you\u2019re already connected to Milton.<br /> <br /> Then you get a description of the Sept you\u2019re gonna be dealing with in these three adventures. It\u2019s called the \u201cSept of the Far Watcher\u201d And imagine my surprise when it starts like this: \u201cIt\u2019s an axiom among the Garou that there are not enough werewolves to fight all their enemies.\u201d Remember the Storyteller\u2019s Kit chronicle where I talked about how it felt like the real issue is a lack of numbers? Well, here it gets spelled out and it definitely is a part of this setting. It\u2019s mentioned at one point: \u201cIn recent years, the name has become a joke among the sept\u2019s members: It covers so much territory, you only see your neighboring packs from afar. In this sense, the sept is more a formality than a community, a tacit agreement of cooperation between packs that don\u2019t meet all that often.\u201d And really, you only get to interact with one Garou during these three adventures until the third adventure when a rival Pack shows up. The way it\u2019s framed it also feels like the idea is that in the present day there are fewer Garou on the planet than, say, fifty years ago. More and more problems arise in the world while at the same time the number of Garou is dwindling year by year.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter Two: The Break Room</span><br /> <br /> <br /> You got three adventures in the book. Theoretically you could take the first two and turn them into stand-alone adventures. The third one definitely requires setup, though, that is delivered by going through the first two adventures. Furthermore, the book helpfully mentions from time-to-time opportunities where you can foreshadow later developments and then in the second/third adventure makes mention of when you can do callbacks to what has come before. So I think the best way to engage with these three adventures is to play them in the order they\u2019re presented in the book.<br /> <br /> Now a word about the art: On one hand, the book has some great visual aids in presenting various locations in the book. The multiple floors of the Val-MOR warehouse or a particular office are depicted in detail. Those are great visual aids. On the other hand, the way it\u2019s presented in the book is absolutely chaotic. For example, the section for getting into the warehouse goes from pg 24 to pg 30. The corresponding image for the warehouse is on pg 31. But get this: The section on entering the dentist\u2019s office goes from pg 30 to pg 34. The corresponding image for that section is on pg 24. It gets even weirder: There\u2019s an actual map of Milton, the city, in the book where all the major locations are marked that you are going to visit in the course of all three adventures. That image can be found on pg 68\u2026 Why?! Additionally, this chaos would make it way too much of a hassle to use that during a session when you have to go through the whole book in the hopes of hitting upon the image somewhere. Making use of those visual aids therefore demands some prep where you copy-paste the images from the pdf, so that they\u2019re easier to go through rather than trying to find them in the book by chance.<br /> <br /> One thing the book also does is that during certain scenes that revolve around interacting with a character, you get these questionnaires with example-questions and what answers said NPC would give. I think it\u2019s a bit of a mixed bag in how helpful it is. The first issue is that the questions are usually very dry and direct. It\u2019s unlikely a player will ask a question that way and then an ST could just read the answer listed in the book verbatim. So, for example, take this bit from the page about interacting with Melissa:<br /> <br /> How long have you been working at the fulfillment center?<br /> Almost a year. It sucks because I got my work-from home job so I could have a more flexible schedule. Sammy\u2019s got a lot of stuff going on. It\u2019s nice to be able to pick him up from school, take him to Little League, and other af ter-school stuff. But it all costs money, so I started working warehouse shifts to be able to afford all that. Other wise, I\u2019m afraid he\u2019s going to melt into the couch and play video games all day.<br /> <br /> Any variations on the questions could mean that this answer has to be phrased differently or that bits of flavor from this answer could be useful in answering a different question. Making use of that on the fly during a session could be a bit of a challenge. Then there\u2019s also the problem that occasionally there\u2019s overlap between answers where I feel like the ST would unintentionally end up repeating themselves by sticking too close to the answers that are listed in the book which would make any dialogue feel less natural.<br /> <br /> Now let\u2019s get to the first adventure. The structure is one of those pearl-beads. There are usually two different routes offered that both lead to the same event. And that process repeats. So, structurally it\u2019s pretty straightforward and all three adventures are very reliant on having a particular NPC guide you through the adventure. There\u2019s always at least one NPC who will give directions to the players as to what they should do and what their goals are supposed to be. Here in the first chapter it\u2019s Mother Louise who is the one Garou you will interact with. Until the rival Pack shows up in the third chapter, there are no other Garou around.<br /> <br /> The first adventure is about Val-MOR corporation which is a mix of Amazon and Walmart. They have a fulfilment-center a la Amazon in Milton but they also have a big-store supermarket a la Walmart in the town. But the warehouse is the focus here. I\u2019m not sure why the supermarket-component was even relevant but okay\u2026<br /> <br /> The corporation is tied to Pentex but it isn\u2019t that Val-MOR is producing Wyrm-tainted stuff or anything. It\u2019s just your usual greedy mega-corporation on that front. Where the Wyrm gets involved is that Val-MOR\u2019s profits have been dropping in the last few years and so Pentex has sent a \u201cRisk Management Specialist\u201d to Milton who\u2019s of course a loyal follower of the Wyrm. And he has this special project that\u2019s supposed to \u201cenhance\u201d workers who struggle \u2013 but instead it\u2019s slowly turning them into insectoid zombie-husks/Fomori.<br /> <br /> I mean, as far as plans go, it\u2019s a really stupid one, I gotta say\u2026 Sure, these zombie-husks are great monsters to throw at werewolves but now you can only put them to work during the night-shift and make sure that no normal person sees these mutated Fomori. And these Fomori are of course far less capable than an actual human at doing normal work. Not sure how that\u2019s supposed to enhance the performance of the warehouse.<br /> <br /> If I were to run this, I would present that Pentex-guy as a bit of a buffoon who slowly realizes that the spirits he employs to create the Fomori aren\u2019t exactly very interested in helping some corporation increase their profits but instead are more interested in infecting more people and spreading corruption.<br /> <br /> What the chapter is really good at, though, is to consider a lot of options when it comes to how you could get into the warehouse and what sort of scenes you can turn that into. There\u2019s a lot of consideration in offering multiple paths. Of course, never say never, especially when it comes to what players decide to do but the chapter offers a good foundation in running this adventure, I think.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter Three: Shadows On The Prison Wall</span><br /> <br /> At this point, I think it\u2019s clear that W5\u2019s decision to strip away Garou\u2019s natural ability to travel to the Umbra and make it an optional Rite instead was a dumb decision. The Umbra is an integral part of WtA and that is still the case in W5. And since this chapter focuses heavily on the Umbra as you can occasionally expect from a WtA-adventure, I guess, you will always get passages like this at the start: \u201cIf none of the Garou know the Rite of Shadow Passage, Mother Louise offers to teach it to a member of the pack, or (if they lack the experience points to learn a Rite) to invoke it on their behalf. Being able to travel in and out of the Umbra of their own volition is a huge benefit in this story, so if a player wants to learn this rite immediately and pay it off with experience points at the end of the story, let them.\u201d You know what? At that point, just give the Rite to all the PCs and don\u2019t make them buy it with XP. There\u2019s no reason to have the game make STs and players jump through hoops like this because of a bad game-design-decision. Just give it to everyone for free and now nobody needs to figure out what to do with PC-Packs that can\u2019t go into the Umbra because no PC has that particular Rite. It\u2019s unnecessary busywork. But I guess, it will needlessly continue to eat up wordcount in future books of the W5 line.<br /> <br /> This chapter is about the group encountering a particular spirit of stories in the Umbra who calls himself the Wizened Raconteur. The introduction is pretty cool because this spirit explains to the Garou that the Umbra is suffering and that there are four different challenges the PCs have to complete to improve things. He\u2019s very vague in what he wants the Garou to do\u2026 BUT in exchange for stories, he will give the PCs more hints. The only issue I could see here is that if you have a starting-group who really only have interacted with that first adventure, the PCs don\u2019t have a lot of stories to share really.<br /> <br /> Structurally it\u2019s also interesting because the four challenges correspond to that axis-map from pg 212 in the W5 corebook. So you get this: \u201c\u2018A Hint of Malice\u2019 is an individual active antagonist scene; \u2018Polyphemus Security Solutions\u2019 is a systemic active antagonist scene; \u2018Reaching for the Sky\u2019 is a passive individual scene; and finally \u2018The Suffering\u2019 is a passive systemic scene.\u201d These can be tackled in any order.<br /> <br /> The first three all have an interesting gimmick. Hint of Malice has you battle against a spirit that gets stronger the more dots in Rage your character has. I think I would have to see that in action how well this actually works. But it\u2019s an interesting idea. Polyphemus Security Solutions has you go up against a security-company that is tied to Pentex. What\u2019s interesting here is that it really builds on the idea that there are approaches/solutions to problems based on the three Renown-categories. To earn Glory, you just go in and beat them all up or kill them to drive the security-firm out of town. To earn Wisdom, you sneak in, hack their computers, you sabotage their equipment and you use social manipulation to set the people working for the firm against each other. To earn Honor, you rally the local business owners and local activists to protest the firm who then will voluntarily leave. Now what you might already notice in what I describe here is the book talking about actions taken by players in these VERY broad outlines. We\u2019ll get back to that in a bit\u2026 The third adventure is about freeing a spirit that\u2019s at the top of the Milton clock tower in the Umbra. And what\u2019s interesting here is that depending on how you free the spirits, its nature changes. So, in what the players choose to do, they\u2019re shaping the form of the spirit.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the fourth adventure \u201cThe Suffering\u201d\u2026 I mean, they kinda wrote themselves into that corner by wanting to adhere to that axis-model from the W5 corebook. The example from the corebook for \u201cpassive systemic\u201d is climate change. Try packing that into a little adventure\u2026 And this book\u2019s solution is to simply don\u2019t. Conceptually you can kinda see why it\u2019s like that but just pragmatically in what it expects STs to do it\u2019s just half-assed. What this section proposes is that there\u2019s this list of systemic issues in Milton: unhoused people, racism, far right extremists, bad politicans\u2026 And your PC group is supposed to fix two of them\u2026 somehow. Here\u2019s an example: \u201cAiding the unhoused: Milton has a small community of unhoused people, centered on a tent city on the outskirts of town. Local politicians consider unhoused people a blight on the town and give the police wide leeway to displace and arrest them, as well as all but eliminating resources to help them. Garou can strike up relationships with the unhoused, support local initiatives to provide housing and assistance, or just gift them a few warm meals. This is an especially relevant approach for Bone Gnawers, who often live in similar hardscrabble circumstances.\u201d Damn, provide them housing\u2026?! Gift them a few warm meals\u2026?! I\u2019m sure, nobody has ever thought of that before! This is gonna change everything!<br /> <br /> The big problem here is that what\u2019s outlined there isn\u2019t even a story-seed. And just making the PCs spend hours in a soup-kitchen with nothing extraordinary happening doesn\u2019t add anything of value to the game. You first have to turn this into a story. For example, there\u2019s a Fomor-landlord who has come in and has been buying up buildings and then has thrown out tenants for spurious reasons which has led to the growth of the unhoused population. So, the Garou take out the Fomor, work with human allies who come in, get the building back and get the unhoused people off the street. Quick and easy. But what this fourth adventure does here is so barebones and half-assed that it creates more work for STs in trying to make this work rather than making their job easier.<br /> <br /> Then the chapter ends with the Wizened Raconteur turning on the PCs and attacking them. Him becoming an enemy suddenly isn\u2019t as interesting as the book seems to think it is in my opinion. It\u2019s a weird spirit that you do work for. Since you\u2019ve been doing good stuff in the course of these four short adventures, I guess most people would assume the spirit is a good guy as well. I think the book does enough in helping STs foreshadow it, especially when players offer stories to him in exchange for hints/help. Because as the book notes, this spirit especially loves stories that involve a lot of pain, suffering and despair. But it is a weird spirit at the end of the day. I guess this is another thing where the book is really putting a heavy burden on the ST to make this work.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an interesting gimmick to this fight as well as the spirit is shaping the Umbra around them, creating Bane spirits that attack the PCs and turning the environment against them by constantly narrating what is going on/will happen. But the players can interrupt his narration with narration of their own that the spirit has to accept. So you can do stuff like narrate that his allies turn against him or use his Umbra-shaping abilities against him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Chapter Four: A Pound of Flesh</span><br /> <br /> This is essentially the finale and if you follow the advice in the book, the ST has been consistently dropping hints that until very recently there has been a Garou Pack called the Rakshaks in Milton who just suddenly disappeared. But now they\u2019re back.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s\u2026 weird. Like in the first adventure where I thought the plan of the Pentex-guy didn\u2019t seem especially well-thought-out, I have similar feelings about what\u2019s going on with the Rakshaks.<br /> <br /> Let me just quote from the book what the big idea is: \u201cThe decay of Milton was theirs to handle, and Horned Serpent\u2019s support hinged on the Rakshaks managing it just as the spirit required. Milton was meant to be a controlled learning ground. The Rakshaks were to watch from a distance and determine what would happen if Val-MOR got their way, study how they operate, and find weaknesses they could exploit to fight corporate evil elsewhere. A petri dish, if you will.\u201d<br /> <br /> And the chapter starts with the PCs finding the nearly dead body of Mother Louise because she learned of what Rakshaks were doing and she intentionally recruited the PC-Pack to thwart this plan(without informing the PCs, though, about what was really going on, though\u2026 for whatever reason). It\u2019s unclear to me from how the text describes it whether this plan came from the Horned Serpent or from the Ghost Council Garou Ridhaan. The Horned Serpent expects Ridhaan to acquire more knowledge about the Wyrm and the Horned Serpent even is angry with Mother Louise interrupting Ridhaan\u2019s plan. But also, the plan makes little sense. Val-MOR is a normal greedy corporation. If that Pentex guy hadn\u2019t shown up, nothing overtly supernatural would have occurred there. And in trying to dismantle Pentex\u2019s efforts or confronting a spirits, you learn plenty about them. How is watching from a distance the better way? How many weakpoints will even get exposed if your enemy can just do whatever they want?<br /> <br /> Anyway, eventually the PCs track down the Rakshaks who are in the process of summoning the Horned Serpent. And you learn immediately that Ridhaan is afraid of losing the Horned Serpent\u2019s favor because of how effective the PCs have been in making Milton a better place. The Horned Serpent is pissed off as well when it appears. It says: \u201c\u201cI will have an explanation for the affronts against my domain. Both this night and the previous. I shall hear three speak from each side. Rakshaks, you shall speak first.\u201d<br /> <br /> You know, I always wondered about that writeup of the Ghost Council in the W5 corebook. If you took it literally, it made me wonder why the Ghost Council weren\u2019t considered another fallen Tribe like the Cult of Fenris. I think what this adventure is echoing is this part from the W5 corebook\u2019s section on the Ghost Council (pg 67 \u2013 68): \u201c \u2018The ends justify the means\u2019 usually comes across as a dangerous political doctrine, but for the Ghost Council, finding an answer or opportunity excuses how it\u2019s accomplished. [ \u2026 ] As might be expected, other Garou often view the werewolves of the Ghost Council as having suspect motives. A fair criticism is that Ghost Council concern themselves with solving the \u201chow\u201d of mysteries for the sake of power, with too little regard for the reasons such power manifests in their means of discovery. The pack has the rival\u2019s klaive \u2014 that\u2019s what\u2019s important. Results now, costs later.\u201d Whoever wrote this part of the book took this description from the W5 corebook to heart. But that\u2019s why I always liked the version from JF Sambrano more. Why would anybody put up with these guys? A whole faction that is dedicated to \u201cthe ends justify the means\u201d?! Why would anybody trust these guys\u2026<br /> <br /> So, anyway, back to the adventure\u2026 The Horned Serpent wants to hear explanations for what has happened. The book mentions three arguments that PCs can roll for that rely on Garou-traditions. The first one, interestingly, is to invoke the Litany: \u201cMother Louise broke one tenet of the Litany \u2014 Respect the Territory of Another \u2014 but the Rakshaks broke the very first tenet by failing to Combat the Wyrm Wherever It Dwells and Whenever It Thrives.\u201d This just highlights, though, why the whole plan is weird. Also, if the Horned Serpent was okay with the plan, then it should be okay with Garou ignoring the \u201cCombat the Wyrm etc.\u201d-tenet of the Litany. This shouldn\u2019t be a persuasive argument to the Horned Serpent. The second argument is that Mother Louise should\u2019ve been judged by the Sept rather than being attacked by the Rakshaks. And the third argument is that the PC-Pack didn\u2019t know anything about what was going on. I guess, that one counts. Also, in my mind that brought up another issue in my mind. If the Rakshaks were so invested in watching from the distance in order to acquire knowledge, why didn\u2019t they contact the PC-Pack as soon as they started to interfere with the situation in Milton? Why did they wait this long?<br /> <br /> And even after all that, the Horned Serpent decides that a contest between the two Packs will decide who it sides with. What an asshole! The Horned Serpent just thinks both the Rakshaks and the PC-Pack lack Wisdom, so neither has a right to the territory. The contest is decided by which Pack recruits a Kin in Milton.<br /> <br /> That particular Kin is Gabriella, an artist, who is at the opening of a gallery. Well, shenanigans ensue. Turns out the art of the gallery is used by a particularly nasty Bane Spirit to strengthen itself and find a way to invade the real world. Fighting breaks out and it\u2019s just in this moment that Gabriella undergoes First Change. She\u2019s in Crinos and fights the Rakshaks and the PC-Pack. Depending on how this develops, you\u2019ve got a variety of different endings: Whether Gabriella survives, which Pack she joins (there\u2019s also the option where she asks the Horned Serpent for a third option and it takes her into the Umbra never to be seen again) and whether Ridhaan will lose the support of the Horned Serpent. Also, if the players do especially well, the Horned Serpent heals Mother Louise.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a weird bit in this chapter as well where one of the Rakshak-Garou, Saif, who\u2019s a Silver Fang secretly meets with the PCs to bribe them. He tells them that he has connections and he can set them up with a different bit of territory to watch. All they have to do is just walk away and let Ridhaan repair his relationship with the Horned Serpent. I don\u2019t know\u2026 this just feels a bit off to me. The tone of this scene is just so mundane and modern. It\u2019s the Age of Apocalypse, the Garou Nation has fallen and this guy is running around trying to bribe a Pack of Garou by offering them a territory to defend somewhere far away that he somehow can give them. This is also the only time where the chagrin-mechanic comes up. That\u2019s the mechanic where the ST judges a character for doing something that hurts their Renown and then their Renown gets reduced until they did something to redeem themselves. What\u2019s new here is the idea that if you suffer chagrin that would take your Renown theoretically into the negatives, the PC gets the Adversary Flaw instead because now (somehow) a whole bunch of Garou know that your character has fucked up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Conclusion</span><br /> <br /> There are parts of this Chronicle Book, I really liked. It had some interesting ideas for spirits to battle and how to interact with player-choices. But I think the biggest problem I have with the book is that it isn\u2019t a good starter-chronicle. Both in the sense of being played by people with no experience with WtA and having a ST who\u2019s just a beginner. Especially the latter. I think there are a lot more challenges that a ST gets burdened with in this book that at first glance might not be apparent. The foreshadowing and the callbacks, for example. Absolutely necessary. In the course of these three adventures you end up assembling a whole cast of side-characters. Like the horse-spirit the PCs meet early on in the first adventure. If a player is attached to that character, the book offers little guidance on what they\u2019re up to in a general sense. It\u2019s easy to imagine that players will come up with way more instances of getting these NPCs involved than the few instances that occasionally get mentioned. And as mentioned, occasionally the descriptions in the book get very broad. Playing out what is described will take far more time than the way the book talks about it. Even though the whole point of a book like this one is to help STs with that minutiae.<br /> <br /> From a story-standpoint, I think the first adventure is okay, I quite like most of the second adventure (except for the fourth little mission you do) but I don\u2019t like the third one. It just feels so harebrained. That Pack with this whole \u201cwatching from the distance\u201d-thing only getting involved after everything has already been turned around, Mother Louis not really warning the PC-Pack about what was actually going on (that she was using the PC Pack as pawns for her personal rivalry), the Rakshaks suddenly attacking Mother Louis and then immediately getting a heavyweight like the Horned Serpent involved. It all just feels like a long series of bad ideas. And the worst part: It has nothing to do with the PCs. It all just happens to them. They weren\u2019t there when Mother Louis was attacked, they can\u2019t prevent the Horned Serpent from getting involved and everything else happened before the PCs even arrived in Milton. It\u2019s a bit of a letdown.<br /> <br /> There are bright spots in here but the book certainly doesn\u2019t succeed in being a good introduction-chronicle for beginners. There are a lot of hidden expectations in the descriptions of this book where the ST is expected to carry the weight of making it all work. This is certainly not something you can ask of STs who are beginners!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T22:11:45-07:00","id":1536785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review#post1536743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:<b> It has nothing to do with the PCs. It all just happens to them</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that is one of the oldest criticism in all WOD adventures. PC sit in the coner while the writers OCs hog the spotlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 06-04-2024, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T22:53:28-07:00","id":1536786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536785#post1536785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair that is one of the oldest criticism in all WOD adventures. PC sit in the coner while the writers OCs hog the spotlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only for Vampire. It's particularly jarring for anyone familiar with legacy W:tA material because Werewolf has a track record of doing the exact opposite - Rage Across the Heavens put the Perfect Crinos Born's fate in the hands of the PCs, Past Lives had the PCs discovering important details about historical scenes, and the Rage Across books had room for having you confront things like the Zmei or the Sept of the Trinity Hive as you traipse through the body of a radioactive goth sandworm to deal with that problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T00:21:27-07:00","id":1536787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536785#post1536785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair that is one of the oldest criticism in all WOD adventures. PC sit in the coner while the writers OCs hog the spotlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in this case, it's worse than that because the PCs aren't even bystanders to somebody else's story. These NPCs just show up in this third adventure with these grievances and complaints, take it out on an NPC that the PCs may or may not have a strong connection to and then they summon the Horned Serpent to complain about how it's all other people's fault that their plans didn't work out which the PCs have never heard of or see traces of. What the book tells you to set up is that the Rikshaks used to claim Milton as their territory but then they disappeared suddenly. The story you're dragged into in that part of the book isn't even that interesting - or makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> One way I could see this having stronger ties to W5 would have been to make this third adventure instead about Ridhaan suffering from Hauglosk. His willingness to sacrifice a whole town to supposedly &quot;learn more about the Wyrm&quot; should be Hauglosk-material. For once, they could've had a case of Hauglosk that isn't directly tied to right-wing extremism. But Ridhaan not being a Nazi is probably what made it inconceivable to imagine him suffering from Hauglosk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T00:44:46-07:00","id":1536788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536787#post1536787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> His willingness to sacrifice a whole town to supposedly &quot;learn more about the Wyrm&quot; should be Hauglosk-material. For once, they could've had a case of Hauglosk that isn't directly tied to right-wing extremism. <b>But Ridhaan not being a Nazi is probably what made it inconceivable to imagine him suffering from Hauglosk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />...</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Did You forgot about the drug pusher who teamed up wrym spret from reclamation? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T01:00:54-07:00","id":1536790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536788#post1536788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did You forgot about the drug pusher who teamed up wrym spret from reclamation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, that one... Yeah, but that's what I mean. This plan of turning Milton into some sort of &quot;petri-dish&quot; is exactly the kind of crazy that should be associated with Hauglosk. Although what isn't clear in the book is to what degree the Horned Serpent itself is involved in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T03:00:26-07:00","id":1536791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536790#post1536790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh right, that one... Yeah, but that's what I mean. This plan of turning Milton into some sort of &quot;petri-dish&quot; is exactly the kind of crazy that should be associated with Hauglosk. Although what isn't clear in the book is to what degree the Horned Serpent itself is involved in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I suspect the current team at Renegade has no idea nor given any direction on how to implement Hauglosk narratively. I Suspect that they would retcon the condition to some spiritual infection than any thing intrinsic to being a werewolf if given the chance. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T14:59:31-07:00","id":1536849,"title":"","content":"The final section seems downright weird, especially with the scale creep and Deus Ex Diabolus antagonists. Thanks for making the effort to inform us and taking the hit for us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T18:02:36-07:00","id":1536855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536849#post1536849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The final section seems downright weird, especially with the scale creep and Deus Ex Diabolus antagonists. Thanks for making the effort to inform us and taking the hit for us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is odd because I thought that 5W ed as a whole is moving away from large scale events and focusing on local stories? Like reclamation and BOHN stories is relatively contained to one town while by contrast act three of the adventure involves an rival patron spriet crashing into the plot? <br /> <br /> Like I feel that the left hand isn't talkin to the right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T15:40:52-07:00","id":1536905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536855#post1536855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is odd because I thought that 5W ed as a whole is moving away from large scale events and focusing on local stories? Like reclamation and BOHN stories is relatively contained to one town while by contrast act three of the adventure involves an rival patron spriet crashing into the plot?<br /> <br /> Like I feel that the left hand isn't talkin to the right...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that Patron Spirit part is still baffling to me. For example, that quote I mentioned: &quot;I will have an explanation for the affronts against my domain.&quot; Why is the Horned Serpent calling Milton &quot;its domain&quot;...? That's what I meant by how unclear this is. Because there's no real explanation as to who's doing what. There's also this bit that I haven't mentioned where the book says in a tiny side-bar for that scene where you're supposed to explain yourself: &quot;Any Ghost Council characters in the players\u2019 pack are already familiar with Horned Serpent. They know how to address and appeal to it, which gives their words more weight. They get +2 dice on their test.&quot; I wish the book had gotten into specifics here. What exactly does that even mean? It would have also served to underline what exactly the core-philosophy of the Ghost Council is supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T19:15:25-07:00","id":1536914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536905#post1536905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly I think the answers to all you're questions is that the ghost council is simply not really devouped beyound the write up in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Like I won't be surprised that a writer decide to have the Horned Serpent is pulling the same con as tiger From BOHN only on tribe wide scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 06-08-2024, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T00:14:00-07:00","id":1536942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536914#post1536914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honstly I think the answers to all you're questions is that the ghost council is simply not really devouped beyound the write up in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Like I won't be surprised that a writer decide to have the Horned Serpent pull the same scheme as tiger From BOHN only on tribe wide scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Galestalkers and Ghost Council are good examples of how the new concepts for these Tribes haven't really worked out. Previously the Younger and Older Brother Tribe had a huge place in the metaplot of the game and there was a lot of lore attached to their place in Garou history with the whole Wyld West setting. Then as part of the whole &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-idea they generalized these Tribes and made them more universal. And what was the result? Now neither Book of Hungry Names nor Heart of the Forest: Purgatory have them as playable Tribes. Previously it would have been unthinkable to not give that corner of the WtA-setting at least some attention. Especially if the setting is the US (like in BOHN). But now...? Now the Horned Serpent is just some big spirit that likes learning stuff, I guess... Galestalkers are just werewolves who like hunting. And other than that you don't have to care that much about these two Tribes anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T00:22:32-07:00","id":1536945,"title":"","content":"I also feel it is good to remember that W5 in general is written with a more loose setting in mind than Legacy was. You know how you can play VtM without involving the Caine myth or disputing it? I feel W5 books are written with similar philosophy.<br /> <br /> (Also very similar to Forsaken, naturally.)<br /> <br /> So it could be that THESE Ghost Councillors are that corrupt and THIS Horned Serpent is that arrogant. But that doesn't apply to every member of GC or every Horned Serpent spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T04:11:13-07:00","id":1536976,"title":"","content":"The way it seems to me is that what belonging to a Tribe in W5 means is that you have an individual Garou. And because of that individual's qualities, goals and/or methods, they're able to enter a pact with a Patron-Spirit. When the Spirit agrees, they technically become a member of that Tribe. But in W5 there aren't any inherent shared values and perspectives between members of a Tribe. They're all just Garou who were individually able to make a pact with the same Patron Spirit.<br /> <br /> What doesn't fit, though, is the Horned Serpent's involvement and how it's portrayed in this book. To quote from the book: &quot;For Horned Serpent\u2019s support, the Rakshaks must feed their Patron Spirit knowledge. They\u2019re expected to squeeze every bit of knowledge out of a situation so they may best apply it to future conflicts. As such, the pack\u2019s bond with Horned Serpent demands that they let the decay in Milton progress until they\u2019ve learned everything they can from it, then defeat it themselves.&quot; That's a relationship between Garou and a Patron Spirit that's much more forceful than how I would portray it in my games. Here in this book, the PCs are supposed to take it as a victory that they thwarted a non-fallen tribal Patron-Spirit's plans. I guess, you really have to take it as this just being A Horned Serpent Spirit, not THE Horned Serpent Spirit attached to the Ghost Council Tribe.<br /> <br /> After playing Book of Hungry Names, I also thought what would be fitting for the W5 setting is if the majority of werewolves identify themselves as Garou who have made pacts with various Spirits for Gifts but due to a lack of opportunity and/or knowledge haven't made a pact with any tribal Patron-Spirit. Most of these Garou act alone with the support of human allies. And whole Packs of Garou are a rarity and even rarer are Packs of Garou who have made pacts with Patron-Spirits. That way the setting also feels more like the Garou-society is a fallen one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T05:17:53-07:00","id":1536978,"title":"","content":"W5 treats tribe the same as VtM treats a clan, it is a personal struggle over a communal one. Even Forsaken has a community based on a tribe.<br /> <br /> The garou of W5 truly seem isolated, not just socially but emotionally. Since you can never have another werewolf as your Touchstone and only one wolf, it seems the setting encourages this as well. Even your pack patron is banned from serving as a support network, likely because Touchstones are supposed to be links to 'normalcy.'<br /> <br /> It does explain the world of W5 a lot better than the core, though. It isn't that the werewolves are apathetic, it is that they just don't see the need to complicate matters with other garou. Or that they feel the unity of the Nation was a sham.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:06:23-07:00","id":1537011,"title":"","content":"To summarize-<br /> <br /> Chapter 1) Stuff most STs already know that could have been summarised in a sidebar.<br /> Chapter 2) Universal Brotherhood go blue collar.<br /> Chapter 3) BG1/2 Side Quest Location Puzzle as a Scenario.<br /> Chapter 4) A Mess from start to finish.<br /> <br /> Fair? Or too harsh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:16:32-07:00","id":1537019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537011#post1537011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To summarize-<br /> <br /> Chapter 1) Stuff most STs already know that could have been summarised in a sidebar.<br /> Chapter 2) Universal Brotherhood go blue collar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The UB was always going blue collar if it netted them another body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:28:54-07:00","id":1537023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537019#post1537019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The UB was always going blue collar if it netted them another body.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but their &quot; Eat, Pray, Love&quot; schtick had a certain level of income as its primary target. But as you say, nothing to stop them bundling a bunch of shift workers into a dark room to get turned into Fleshforms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:25:43-07:00","id":1537071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537011#post1537011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To summarize-<br /> <br /> Chapter 1) Stuff most STs already know that could have been summarised in a sidebar.<br /> Chapter 2) Universal Brotherhood go blue collar.<br /> Chapter 3) BG1/2 Side Quest Location Puzzle as a Scenario.<br /> Chapter 4) A Mess from start to finish.<br /> <br /> Fair? Or too harsh?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fair, I think.<br /> <br /> Chapter 1 doesn't add a lot. It's stuff like it proposes a good first question as ST for Session Zero is &quot;Do you have questions about WtA?&quot;. It's really that obvious and surface-level. Like this point in the Session Zero section: &quot;What do you hope to experience from the pack dynamic? (As the Storyteller, you can elaborate on the question to help your troupe: Should the pack have a leader? If yes, what kind of responsibilities do they have? Should everyone have a unique role, or would you prefer a more fluid dynamic?)&quot; The book really lets itself off the hook with this stuff by simply saying &quot;Let the players tell you how they think this should be handled.&quot; instead of delving into Auspices and Tribes and the interplay between them. And then if players want things to be different, sure. But simply expecting players to handle it on their own feels like a cop-out to avoid delving into the WtA-setting. And that then leaves this chapter with advice you pretty much already got from the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Hmm, really could be that Insect Spirits from Shadowrun were the inspiration here. I was wondering why it had to be insects. They got this explanation in that chapter that these insect-Spirits called Vaegesti, are Weaver Spirits corrupted by the Wyrm. Why not pick something more Wyrm-y to begin with?<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's easy to picture Chapter 3 within a videogame. And then it doesn't help that the last adventure is unable to tie it all together in a good way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536978#post1536978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 treats tribe the same as VtM treats a clan, it is a personal struggle over a communal one. Even Forsaken has a community based on a tribe.<br /> <br /> The garou of W5 truly seem isolated, not just socially but emotionally. Since you can never have another werewolf as your Touchstone and only one wolf, it seems the setting encourages this as well. Even your pack patron is banned from serving as a support network, likely because Touchstones are supposed to be links to 'normalcy.'<br /> <br /> It does explain the world of W5 a lot better than the core, though. It isn't that the werewolves are apathetic, it is that they just don't see the need to complicate matters with other garou. Or that they feel the unity of the Nation was a sham.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;Lack of numbers is one of the main-problems for Garou.&quot;-bit also helps, I think. That way it's not necessary to castigate Garou society at every turn (for example, there's still value to things like the Litany) and being an Elder doesn't come with some nebulous inherent moral deficiency (instead it's a result of breaking under the pressure of a worsening situation). With this take can center it all on &quot;There are a lot of problems and not a lot of Garou.&quot;. At least, it's better than the way it's portrayed in the corebook.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:28:17-07:00","id":1537072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536945#post1536945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel it is good to remember that W5 in general is written with a more loose setting in mind than Legacy was. You know how you can play VtM without involving the Caine myth or disputing it? I feel W5 books are written with similar philosophy.<br /> <br /> (Also very similar to Forsaken, naturally.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... But even forsaken provides some loose back story for tribes and how they end up in they current position in the world while by contrast W5 core just doesn't.<br /> <br /> Also Werewolf the: Essentials is taking similar stance to the setting but that doesn't prevent them from writing out a timeline from the start of the garou nation to the game's &quot;present day&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Also funfact WT:E present time frame isn't the age of Apocalypse, its the age of heros)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536978#post1536978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 treats tribe the same as VtM treats a clan, it is a personal struggle over a communal one. Even Forsaken has a community based on a tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact a beta version of OG WTA was going to end up the same way until the play testers find it boring so they pivoted to something more action focused..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 06-09-2024, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T10:46:02-07:00","id":1537090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537072#post1537072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact a beta version of OG WTA was going to end up the same way until the play testers find it boring so they pivoted to something more action focused..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's pretty much it, isn't it? W5 is reinventing the wheel, because the philosophy behind it wanted personal horror like vampire. But in a game with an external focus. So now that W5 is out, so much of the personal horror is found to be bothersome to writing new books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T11:58:33-07:00","id":1537096,"title":"","content":"Fantastic review! Magnificent! It has sold me on the book and explained all of the flaws I'll have to look for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536855#post1536855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is odd because I thought that 5W ed as a whole is moving away from large scale events and focusing on local stories? Like reclamation and BOHN stories is relatively contained to one town while by contrast act three of the adventure involves an rival patron spriet crashing into the plot?<br /> <br /> Like I feel that the left hand isn't talkin to the right...</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I wouldn't be surprised if it ends up exactly like V5.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, we made major changes like getting rid of the Elders. Then we DIALED THE FUCK BACK. Because that was dumb.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T12:01:06-07:00","id":1537097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1536976#post1536976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way it seems to me is that what belonging to a Tribe in W5 means is that you have an individual Garou. And because of that individual's qualities, goals and/or methods, they're able to enter a pact with a Patron-Spirit. When the Spirit agrees, they technically become a member of that Tribe. But in W5 there aren't any inherent shared values and perspectives between members of a Tribe. They're all just Garou who were individually able to make a pact with the same Patron Spirit..</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that doesn't seem to be the case. The tribes have broadly shared values.<br /> <br /> Like Black Furies are JUSTICE.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs are still, &quot;Born better, better than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T12:45:47-07:00","id":1537099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537097#post1537097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, that doesn't seem to be the case. The tribes have broadly shared values.<br /> <br /> Like Black Furies are JUSTICE.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs are still, &quot;Born better, better than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but compared to the way Legacy AND Forsaken handled tribes, W5 is much closer to how clans in VtM work. Previously, to join a tribe you needed to find tribe members and prove your worth to them. You could not join a tribe without being tasked by your future peers.<br /> <br /> In W5, seen in the example characters, to join a tribe you basically just have to impress the patron and no other task is needed. Hence why a head of a state and a monk can be tribed garou, because it is personal.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I feel it is even more isolated than clans in VtM, because Embrace at least requires another vampire. Joining a tribe in W5 can be done on your own.<br /> <br /> This lack of community is pretty weird, given how important packs are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 06-09-2024, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T12:49:15-07:00","id":1537102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537097#post1537097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, that doesn't seem to be the case. The tribes have broadly shared values.<br /> <br /> Like Black Furies are JUSTICE.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs are still, &quot;Born better, better than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emphasis is on &quot;broad&quot; in W5, though. Black Furies are a prime example of this. You have an individual Garou and if they truly care about justice they're able to make a pact with Gorgon which then makes them a Black Fury. But questions of what exactly justice is and matters like what is righteous to do in the name of justice and what not... All of that is entirely individualized. You ask two Black Furies about what justice is and you get two different answers. That's what I mean.<br /> <br /> W5 Tribes are way broader than WtA Tribes, not just in concept but also in prioritizing individuals over the community. Tribe has much less communal value in W5 than in previous editions. Being of the same Tribe is of little value in W5 when it comes to companionship and shared identity. The things people of the same Tribe share in W5 are so broad that the individual identity matters more than being a member of any Tribe.<br /> <br /> In this book's third adventure Ghost Council PCs are just having an easier time convincing the Horned Serpent that Ridhaan (who's also a Ghost Council member) is wrong. Although I wonder how this would land with players when they hear about the relationship between Ridhaan and the Horned Serpent when one of the PCs is also a Ghost Council Garou. Because that moment would land very differently if you don't ascribe to the notion I outlined above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:07:15-07:00","id":1537105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537099#post1537099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do, but compared to the way Legacy AND Forsaken handled tribes, W5 is much closer to how clans in VtM work. <b>Previously, to join a tribe you needed to find tribe members and prove your worth to them. You could not join a tribe without being tasked by your future peers.</b><br /> <br /> In W5, seen in the example characters, to join a tribe you basically just have to impress the patron and no other task is needed. Hence why a head of a state and a monk can be tribed garou, because it is personal.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I feel it is even more isolated than clans in VtM, because Embrace at least requires another vampire. Joining a tribe in W5 can be done on your own.<br /> <br /> This lack of community is pretty weird, given how important packs are.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Re. Bold.</b><br /> <br /> Kinda............socially you proved your worth to Tribe Members <u>but </u> they had zero say over whether or not you were a Tribe Member thats 100% up to the Matron/Patron.......though Tribe Members do have a fair bit of say over how difficult life as a Member will be....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:20:28-07:00","id":1537107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537105#post1537105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Re. Bold.</b><br /> <br /> Kinda............socially you proved your worth to Tribe Members <u>but </u> they had zero say over whether or not you were a Tribe Member thats 100% up to the Matron/Patron.......though Tribe Members do have a fair bit of say over how difficult life as a Member will be....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but depending on the sept you couldn't get a RoP unless they saw you as ready for the tribe.<br /> <br /> There was a heavy factor of proving even before Rite of Passage that W5 lacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:39:55-07:00","id":1537115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537107#post1537107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but depending on the sept you couldn't get a RoP unless they saw you as ready for the tribe.<br /> <br /> There was a heavy factor of proving even before Rite of Passage that W5 lacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the lack of politics in what was one of the most political games.....honestly Garou and Changeling politics make Vamp politics look like model UN....is rather saddening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-09-2024, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T06:25:09-07:00","id":1537148,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537090#post1537090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's pretty much it, isn't it? W5 is reinventing the wheel, because the philosophy behind it wanted personal horror like vampire. But in a game with an external focus. So now that W5 is out, so much of the personal horror is found to be bothersome to writing new books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... Honestly I suspect that a couple of supplements later the writers would decide to have the garous from into scattered communities and maybe flirt with the idea of the PCs reforming Garou nation or at the very least having they actions from the foundation for it's replacement..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537115#post1537115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the lack of politics in what was one of the most political games.....honestly Garou and Changeling politics make Vamp politics look like model UN....is rather saddening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah seriously werewolf the essentials version of the garou looks like a utopia in comparison. Like sure the nation is split but both sides still acknowledge that they fight for Gaia. Just via different means. As far as the writers of WT:E is concerned the age of apocalypse has passed. Now it's the age of hero's where garous old and new rise up and save Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 06-11-2024, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T01:34:28-07:00","id":1537472,"title":"","content":"Renegade has started releasing previews for Scent Of Decay, so I can show off one part of what I mentioned in my original review: The first chapter. What's weird is that before you would get the product-page, then the cover-reveal, then various pages from the book as previews and then eventually the pre-order pdf would be released. This time around the pre-order-pdf was released before they started releasing the previews of various pages from the book. I wonder if they're going to continue doing it in this new order now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, these are four pages from the first chapter and these are all you get for the advice-part on Session Zero and Pack dynamics. The focus was too much on general advice which you already got from the corebook and not nearly enough on WtA-specific dynamics.<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1533\" height=\"945\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/v6st8WJ.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/v6st8WJ.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/v6st8WJ.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1566\" height=\"945\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/CvAPWK2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/CvAPWK2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/CvAPWK2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> Looking at it again, I also wonder why they have that page on &quot;Unusual Packs&quot; in this book. The upcoming Shattered Nation supplement blurb mentions a discussion of Pack Types. So why would you put this page on Auspice-focused Pack Types in this Chronicle book? And it's not like the three adventures lent themselves to having Auspice-focused Packs. In fact, they even offhandedly mention at one point how different Auspices will shine at different moments during the three adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T07:52:09-07:00","id":1537488,"title":"","content":"I mean ' Unusual' Packs is pretty much Normal Packs, its pretty rare theres a perfect 5 member Pack with one of each Auspice unless theres some sort of prophecy in place.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the 'advice' there is basically ' be a semi-functional ST'....which, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T13:33:54-07:00","id":1537522,"title":"","content":"OFC they float having two or more Galliards as the basis of a band. I mean, if no one's an Ahroun, who's going to play the drums? And why did they stop capitalizing Auspice names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T02:38:19-07:00","id":1537551,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's true... they're pitching &quot;Galliards as musicians&quot;... again!<br /> <br /> For context: JF Sambrano told that story of how during the writing-process for the Hunters Entertainment version the writers were mostly going the route of Galliards as lorekeepers/historians whenever it came up for the example archetypes in the Tribe-sections and then Karim Muammar asked them to mix it up. But then in the released W5 corebook we got you had the opposite issue of it pretty much being nothing but Galliards as musicians. And now the Galliard-Pack-Type once again focuses on the musician-aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T18:22:22-07:00","id":1537592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537551#post1537551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that's true... they're pitching &quot;Galliards as musicians&quot;... again!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair musical traditions is a form of record keeping among many cultures, though I suspect that Parawolf might not get that nuance...<br /> <br /> Really it's odd that a &quot;historian&quot; Pack type is all Philodox since having a Galliard around would be handy for identifying any oral tradition and well the Galliard would have new materials so it's a win-win.<br /> <br /> Also unrelated but anyone wants to make a thread about Werewolf the: Essentials. Like by god this forum needs have something positive to to talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T06:04:42-07:00","id":1537697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537592#post1537592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also unrelated but anyone wants to make a thread about Werewolf the: Essentials. Like by god this forum needs have something positive to to talk about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I searched for it thanks to your posts.<br /> So far it's a good and positive reading experience, and something I needed to read<br /> You should definitely open a thread. But if you are the author of WtE and feel embarassed about opining it yourself, I can do it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T01:47:59-07:00","id":1537813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537697#post1537697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I searched for it thanks to your posts.<br /> So far it's a good and positive reading experience, and something I needed to read<br /> You should definitely open a thread. But if you are the author of WtE and feel embarassed about opining it yourself, I can do it</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no I don't mind you opening a thread about WtE. I don't really have the energy or time to talk about a fan line.<br /> <br /> Also to be clear I'm not the main author of WtE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T13:22:02-07:00","id":1537877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review#post1536743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of hidden expectations in the descriptions of this book where the ST is expected to carry the weight of making it all work. </div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a plague in many an RPG chronicle. In WoD since always. Too bad it still hounds this chronicle.<br /> Actually, much of the system and setting of WoD does that, even with 5th edition making it a lot more manageable and giving many new tools to help it, it still has this problem. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T13:36:07-07:00","id":1537901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536743-w5-scent-of-decay-review?p=1537877#post1537877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been a plague in many an RPG chronicle. In WoD since always. Too bad it still hounds this chronicle.<br /> Actually, much of the system and setting of WoD does that, even with 5th edition making it a lot more manageable and giving many new tools to help it, it still has this problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have weighed this so much if this book hadn't presented itself as a &quot;starter-chronicle&quot;, in other words, something newbies in the realms of STs and players are expected to use and/or experience. And even then, I think the text presents challenges that go way beyond what is described in the book. Take the &quot;Wizened Raconteur&quot; from Chapter 3: You have a Spirit who gives out four quests where the PCs will do good but after all of that it turns out the Spirit is evil. That's easier said than done. You make the Spirit too evil as ST and the PCs could potentially want to confront the Spirit instead after one or two tasks, thereby skipping parts of that chapter. You make him too nice and the turn won't land. You might get some blank stares or confused/angry reactions of &quot;Wait, what?!&quot;. How to strike the balance and avoid these two scenarios is exactly the kind of thing you should put into the book and yet that isn't happening here.<br /> <br /> The second chapter/first adventure comes closest to a good presentation of a pre-written adventure (although even there are some moments where things heavily rely on the ST to manage things). The third chapter/second adventure has some bright spots. And I think that the fourth chapter/third adventure that follows that is just a mess. I have some serious doubts this third adventure would work as described once you involve actual players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}